{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/874378-musing-on-sidereal-martial-arts","id":874378,"title":"Musing on Sidereal Martial Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T03:17:56-07:00","id":874378,"title":"Musing on Sidereal Martial Arts","content":"Had a brainstorm while drowsing, about the shape of Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> Since they can't be what they were- 'just' a very high essence charm set- because the Essence 6+ range is explicitly... if not verbotten, at least sufficiently uncommon as to not meaningfully drive play. And that got me thinking about one of Jenna's comments, re: SMA from way back forever ago- <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zaraborgstrom/WhenToLearnSMA\" target=\"_blank\">Thus Spak Zaraborgstrom...</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jenna Moran</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">That's a good middle ground. I was going to do that before I decided it was more elegant to jeer at people who learned secret styles before learning a single basic martial arts Charm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">[[ Or, rather, because it seemed to me that you could pick up the first secret Charms before learning a complete tree, but that mandating going to a Form-type Charm first would encourage people to do it in exactly that order---rather than thinking about when a good time to get the secret styles Charms is, they'd grab a Form to &quot;let&quot; them get to the secret styles, then grab a bunch of secret style Charms, then grumblingly go back to the main tree, then get the secret Form. I figured that the psychology was more likely to work to my advantage if I just left it open---either you grab one early and that's your &quot;trick&quot;, because it's awfully expensive and you don't have enough MA to work with, really . . . or you grab one when you and your sifu realize that it's time. ]]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Rebecca<br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><br /> <br /> These are leading me to the following conceptualization of what it takes to learn an SMA Charm.<br /> <br /> * Sidereals can learn one Sidereal Martial Arts Charm at Essence 1, one at Essence 3, and one at Essence 5.<br /> * Sidereals can learn an additional Sidereal Martial Arts Charm for each Prayer Strip charm they have acquired within their own trees.<br /> * Sidereals, Solars and Abyssals can learn one Sidereal Martial Arts Charm for each Martial Arts style they have mastered.<br /> * Sidereal Martial Arts charms typically use the Martial Arts ability unless specified otherwise, but often require mastery over another ability to learn. There is not a distinct style to mundanely practice; no Martial Arts (Prismatic Arrangement of Creation) like there is Martial Arts (Snake).<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">* Sidereal Martial Arts charms do not have the Terrestrial or Mastery keywords.</span></span><br /> * In all cases, the student must <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">still meet all other requirements for the charm.<br /> <br /> This would obviously mean a massive trimming down of the SMA styles as they exist- most such 'Styles' would probably be around 3 to 5 charms, and there could be several individual 'points of enlightenment' that neither require nor lead to further charms.<br /> <br /> So, for example (and very off the cuff)-</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inconsolata\"><span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Four Magical Materials Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 15m; <b>Mins:</b> Craft 5, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The martial artist knows the future hidden within starmetal; she has learned the dance of moonsilver; she has braved the heat in the volcano-forge from which rises orihalcum; she has befriended the five authorities of jade. With these truths, she transforms herself into a living artifact.<br /> <br /> While the martial artist is in the Four Magical Materials Form, treat her unarmed attacks as Medium Artifact Weapons with the Lethal, Brawl, Grappling, and Natural tags. Increase her natural soak by +8, and increase her Hardness to 7 if it is less than 7.<br /> <br /> As a living artifact, the martial artist may even develop evocations as they are draw more deeply on the bond between themselves and the four magical materials. These evocations are only usable while in the form.<br /> <br /> The Four Magical Materials Form cannot be used while in armor or while wielding a weapon.</span></span><br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T04:58:54-07:00","id":874410,"title":"","content":"An interesting idea. It's a completely different approach to SMAs than any others I've seen and I look forward to seeing where it goes.<br /> <br /> Where Charms use the Martial Arts ability will they require a 'generic' Martial Arts or will they key off of the highest Martial Arts ability that the user has? Also for a Sidereal who has zero Martial Arts dots or charms (which seems to be possible with your approach) would they just be at a severe disadvantage compared to one who does? Or would there be an alternative way to use such charms? (Or even alternative SMAs that key off of other abilities?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:02:36-07:00","id":874413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/874378-musing-on-sidereal-martial-arts?p=874410#post874410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting idea. It's a completely different approach to SMAs than any others I've seen and I look forward to seeing where it goes.<br /> <br /> Where Charms use the Martial Arts ability will they require a 'generic' Martial Arts or will they key off of the highest Martial Arts ability that the user has? Also for a Sidereal who has zero Martial Arts dots or charms (which seems to be possible with your approach) would they just be at a severe disadvantage compared to one who does? Or would there be an alternative way to use such charms? (Or even alternative SMAs that key off of other abilities?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect they would usually key off the martial artist's highest martial arts ability; how does it work now if you have multiple martial arts abilities at different ratings and make an attack enhanced by charms of multiple styles?<br /> <br /> Re: Sidereal with zero martial arts.<br /> <br /> I imagine they'd get less use out of many of the SMA charms then- but, as a for instance, the above Four Magical Materials Form would be just fine for a Sidereal with some dots in Brawl without any particular Martial Arts training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:04:58-07:00","id":874462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/874378-musing-on-sidereal-martial-arts?p=874413#post874413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I expect they would usually key off the martial artist's highest martial arts ability; how does it work now if you have multiple martial arts abilities at different ratings and make an attack enhanced by charms of multiple styles?<br /> <br /> Re: Sidereal with zero martial arts.<br /> <br /> I imagine they'd get less use out of many of the SMA charms then- but, as a for instance, the above Four Magical Materials Form would be just fine for a Sidereal with some dots in Brawl without any particular Martial Arts training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently you use the highest rating when mixing multiple styles, but I wanted to check rather than assume anything. Would be interested in seeing some more charms though to see how you think the structure would work. Do you think that charms within a single style will all require the same base ability? (Will all of PAoC use Craft?) Or will they require a stylist to be diverse to master a style?<br /> <br /> One last thing. Are you concerned at all about potentially putting relatively high-powered charms within easy reach of a starting Sidereal? I would expect the charm you've used as an example above to be a E3 charm (roughly), but any Sid could take it in chargen if they wanted (assuming I've understood everything correctly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My attempt at a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15dK8fZaL-Kn-yGKxW6VRg_z6aF27FqbIf-t8ZEXmMC4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal 3e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8793-grifftofer","name":"Grifftofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"104"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T06:33:49-07:00","id":874486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grifftofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/874378-musing-on-sidereal-martial-arts?p=874462#post874462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Currently you use the highest rating when mixing multiple styles, but I wanted to check rather than assume anything. Would be interested in seeing some more charms though to see how you think the structure would work. Do you think that charms within a single style will all require the same base ability? (Will all of PAoC use Craft?) Or will they require a stylist to be diverse to master a style?<br /> <br /> One last thing. Are you concerned at all about potentially putting relatively high-powered charms within easy reach of a starting Sidereal? I would expect the charm you've used as an example above to be a E3 charm (roughly), but any Sid could take it in chargen if they wanted (assuming I've understood everything correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Ability diversity.<br /> <br /> I expected it would vary by style, but err on the side of diversity. Prismatic Arrangement of Creation I would see as using Crafts, Occult, Performance, Lore, and Martial Arts (any) (for 4MMF, Soul Fire Shaper Form, Games of Divinity Form, Manse and Demense Form and Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form). CMoS, OTOH, I would see as being only maybe three-ish Charms- and probably depend on Athletics and/or Brawl. (Haven't considered it deeply enough to decide yet). No idea about even trying something like Obsidian Shards of Bullshit.<br /> <br /> Re: Powerful<br /> <br /> They could; they could also take a medium artifact weapon and armor. Which is to say- not every SMA would be Essence 1, and a character having a secret technique that is disproportionately powerful and expensive is exactly the kind of 'trick' that Jenna was speaking towards, which is part of what set my mind rolling down this path. On average, I'd expect SMA Charms to 'feel' like Essence +1 or +2 Charms, owing to their greater scarcity and limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}